"89999f085b1c269cdb7206ca806d5ef65c1b1211", "format": "Archive BitTorrent"}, {"name": "UnderWesternStars_files.xml", "source": "original", "format": "Metadata", "md5": "a48a4e6973294ec2095ea13621cb1eb5", "summation": "md5"}, {"name": "UnderWesternStars_meta.xml", "source": "original", "format": "Metadata", "mtime": "1762236746", "size": "1390", "md5": "a0d2c8eb451987659f21290e7c6b3096", "crc32": "96eec386", "sha1": "55a1f13cde17c0eb73dfba81e980866f4ab69bec"}, {"name": "UnderWesternStars_reviews.xml", "source": "original", "mtime": "1661287864", "size": "1433", "md5": "024a52159364a0904673f0d353b3cab6", "crc32": "dc932564", "sha1": "d065cb48371a3a4e32de6d72e1923ec1ab2e3d7a", "format": "Metadata"}, {"name": "__ia_thumb.jpg", "source": "original", "mtime": "1657984804", "size": "6176", "md5": "8488d5e896ea6632640c87ce18e197ec", "crc32": "0b216bb4", "sha1": "59ca1ac96f78327eaa3d4959d2dc323d104b2a59", "format": "Item Tile", "rotation": "0"}], "files_count": 75, "item_last_updated": 1762236754, "item_size": 1726917242, "metadata": {"identifier": "UnderWesternStars", "title": "Under Western Stars", "creator": "Sol C. Siegel", "mediatype": "movies", "collection": ["feature_films_unsorted", "feature_films", "moviesandfilms"], "description": "Roy Rogers plays the son of a late Congressman who fought on behalf of the small ranchers who are being starved out because of the dam the water power company has built and the exorbitant rates being charged.\n\nThis was the first Movie that Leonard Sly starred in as Roy Rogers", "date": "1938", "year": "1938", "subject": "Western; Romance; Roy Rogers", "licenseurl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/mark/1.0/", "publicdate": "2011-05-30 07:36:54", "addeddate": "2011-05-30 07:34:16", "uploader": "josef_schrantz@freenet.de", "director": "Joseph Kane", "publisher": "Republic Pictures", "sound": "sound", "color": "black & white", "runtime": "65 min.", "contact": "www.k-otic.com", "updatedate": "2011-05-30 07:45:11", "updater": "k-otic", "backup_location": "ia903700_14", "collection_added": ["feature_films", "moviesandfilms"]}, "reviews": [{"reviewbody": "In early 1938, after filming was completed on \"The Old Barn Dance\", Gene Autry informed Herbert J. Yates, head of Republic Pictures that he was going on strike for a laundry list of things. What to do? \"Under Western Stars\" was in pre-production and was close to a date to shoot. Leonard Slye as \"Dick Weston\" had made an impression on Autry's previous picture and was brought in as a substitute renamed Roy Rogers. A few changes were made to frame the new star better and it was a little longer and with somewhat better production values than Autry was getting. It was released on 04-20-1938 and was a smash hit. \"Dust\" was nominated for an Oscar for song of the year, as well. Autry and Yates came to terms after that and a new Western Star was born. The film has been added to the govt. film preservation registry in recent years. It's a very sturdy little modern day western. A MUST SEE even. The uncut version has good picture and sound quality too. Enjoy", "reviewtitle": "My 103rd Review A Gene Autry Picture Without Autry", "reviewer": "bobsluckycat", "reviewdate": "2011-06-11 16:14:27", "createdate": "2011-06-11 16:14:27", "stars": "5"}], "server": "dn801202.us.archive.org", "simplelists": {"solo_manifest": {"solo_manifest_dn801202": {"sys_changed_by": {"source": "task", "task_id": "5461199200"}, "sys_last_changed": "2026-06-23 12:47:10.764074"}}}, "solo": true, "uniq": 1367002005, "workable_servers": ["dn801202.us.archive.org"]}